{
  "info": {
    "name": "Kairox CMS",
    "description": "CMS (kx.cms): content reads for the website and the editors' admin API. Generated by scripts/gen_handoff.py from the code; read docs/handoff/CMS_API.md. Pick the Kairox local or staging environment. Sign in once (folder 01); the collection then renews the staff token by itself.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{access_token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "buyer_text",
      "value": "Hi, I need 50,000 aluminium containers 750 ml with lids, delivery to Dubai."
    },
    {
      "key": "web_text",
      "value": "Hello, do you make aluminium food containers with lids?"
    },
    {
      "key": "wa_reuse_last_id",
      "value": "no"
    },
    {
      "key": "cms_operation",
      "value": "publish"
    },
    {
      "key": "cms_age_seconds",
      "value": "0"
    },
    {
      "key": "export_entity",
      "value": "deals"
    },
    {
      "key": "setting_value",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "00 Health and keys",
      "description": "Is the server up? Run these first on every target.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check (API up)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/healthz",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Liveness: the API process answers.\n\n**Who may call it:** public (monitoring)\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Health check (scheduler and workers)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/healthz/beat",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "healthz",
                "beat"
              ]
            },
            "description": "D46: UptimeRobot checks this from outside; 503 = Beat, the broker or the workers stopped (or the oldest due job is waiting too long).\n\n**Who may call it:** public (monitoring)\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Public key for staff tokens (JWKS)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/.well-known/jwks.json",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                ".well-known",
                "jwks.json"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The public key that verifies staff access tokens (RS256, D26).\n\n**Who may call it:** public\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200",
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "01 Staff sign-in and MFA",
      "description": "Sign in with email + password, then a second step. First sign-in: email code, change the one-time password, enrol YOUR OWN authenticator app, then sign in again with the app.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Login (email + password)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step 1: email + password. Answers the second steps on offer (TOTP first; email code fallback).\n\n**Who may call it:** public (no sign-in)\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{staff_email}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{staff_password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.environment.set(\"challenge_token\", d.challenge_token);",
                  "  pm.test(\"Second step offered: \" + d.methods.join(\", \"), function () { pm.expect(d.methods.length).to.be.above(0); });",
                  "  console.log(d.totp_enrolled ? \"Next: 7. Second step with the authenticator code\" : \"Next: 2. Send the email sign-in code\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Send the email sign-in code",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/mfa/email/send",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "mfa",
                "email",
                "send"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Fallback second step: a 6-digit code to the staff member's work address (valid 10 minutes).\n\n**Who may call it:** public (no sign-in)\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 204",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"challenge_token\": \"{{challenge_token}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 204\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(204); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Verify the email code (first sign-in / fallback)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/mfa/email/verify",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "mfa",
                "email",
                "verify"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Step 2 with the email code: signed in with `mfa=false` (no approvals until TOTP is used).\n\n**Who may call it:** public (no sign-in)\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"challenge_token\": \"{{challenge_token}}\",\n  \"code\": \"{{email_code}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.environment.set(\"access_token\", d.access_token);",
                  "  if (d.expires_in) { pm.environment.set(\"access_expires_at\", String(Date.now() + d.expires_in * 1000)); }",
                  "  const rc = pm.cookies.get(\"kx_refresh\");",
                  "  if (rc) { pm.environment.set(\"refresh_token\", rc); }  // rotates on every renewal (auto-renew script)",
                  "  pm.environment.set(\"token_\" + d.user.role + (d.mfa ? \"\" : \"_emailcode\"), d.access_token);",
                  "  pm.environment.set(\"me_user_id\", d.user.id);",
                  "  pm.test(\"Signed in as \" + d.user.role + \" (mfa=\" + d.mfa + \")\", function () { pm.expect(d.access_token).to.be.a(\"string\"); });",
                  "  if (d.must_change_password) { console.warn(\"must_change_password=true: run '4. Change password' next\"); }",
                  "  if (!d.totp_enrolled) { console.warn(\"No authenticator yet: run '5. Enrol your authenticator app' next\"); }",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Change password (first sign-in: replace the one-time password)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/password",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "password"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Change the password (ends every other session).\n\n**Who may call it:** any signed-in staff\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 204",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"current_password\": \"{{staff_password}}\",\n  \"new_password\": \"{{new_password}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 204\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(204); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 204) {",
                  "  console.log(\"Password changed. Copy new_password into staff_password in your environment, then run 1. Login again.\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Enrol your authenticator app (shows a QR code)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/v1/auth/totp/enrol",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "v1",
                "auth",
                "totp",
                "enrol"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A new authenticator seed for the signed-in user (active only after /totp/confirm). Replacing an active authenticator needs a TOTP sign-in (D4) and the user is told by email.\n\n**Who may call it:** any signed-in staff\n\n**Expected on success:** HTTP 200"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status is 200\", function () { pm.response.to.have.status(200); });",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json();",
                  "  const tpl = `<div style=\"font-family:sans-serif;padding:8px\"><p>Scan this QR code with your authenticator app",
                  "  (Google Authenticator, Microsoft Authenticator, 1Password ...), or type the key by hand.</p>",
                  "  <div id=\"qr\"></div><p>Key: <code>{{secret}}</code></p>",
                  "  <script src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/qrcodejs/1.0.0/qrcode.min.js\"></script>",
                  "  <script>pm.getData(function (err, data) { new QRCode(document.getElementById(\"qr\"), data.uri); });</script></div>`;",
                  "  pm.visualizer.set(tpl, { uri: d.otpauth_uri, secret: d.secret });",
                  "  console.log(\"Open the Visualize tab of this response to scan the QR code. Then put the 6-digit code in totp_code and run 6.\");",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
